  "limits": [
    "Native formula applied to existing local age and indexed random inputs; native RNG/clock producers and live FPCR remain unobserved.",
    "Half nearest-even is an explicit local policy. Ray colors follow the distinct clamped float32 byte path and the observed normalized vertex format; no native game or Metal shader execution.",
    "Only the private primary ray opts into the normalized BGRA stream. Its source mode 4, white omitted modulation factor and unit UV/no-multiplier specialization are guarded. Other families retain their existing packet and shading policies.",
    "The first native 28-byte layout and default quad shader compose conditionally; native draw-specific selection, record producers and live FPCR remain unobserved. This is not a complete native visual parity certificate.",
    "Final GPU comparisons use actual runtime geometry/material code and an independent normalized Uint8 attribute reference from C/Python packet values. The omitted ray lookup texture uses the production white fallback.",
    "The default placement timing loop is retained only for exact numerical/ownership equivalence on unrequested paths; no new performance or game-FPS claim is made.",
    "The historical Leona archive closure and default-platform Lux golden remain the same two full-suite failures; no golden, assertion or wave deadline was weakened."
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "An initial integration expectation guessed the ray alpha byte as 123. The unchanged source curve and independent C reference establish byte 198 at time 0.08; the expectation was corrected without changing curve evaluation.",
    "The first GPU setup assumed the ray had an authored lookup texture; it instead uses the production white fallback. A failed text replacement briefly left the probe white variable undefined; an explicit patch corrected the fixture.",
    "A provisional float-uniform representation differed from normalized vertex attributes by one channel byte at one pixel (time 0.1, runtime blend, 64 target). The final path stores actual normalized BGRA bytes and retains zero-difference acceptance; source colors stay unquantized.",
    "The full suite and final nine-case browser run were repeated after adopting the actual byte attribute. Earlier provisional logs remain diagnostics, not the final certificate."
  ],
